# HP OMEN MAX per-key RGB keyboard (HID LampArray, Usage Page 0x59).
#
# The keyboard exposes five hidraw nodes; four of them carry keystrokes and
# must stay root-only. Only interface 4 is the LampArray control channel, so
# the interface number has to be part of the match.
#
# This cannot be written with ATTRS{}: udev requires every ATTRS{} key in a
# rule to match on one single parent, and idVendor/idProduct live on the USB
# device while bInterfaceNumber lives on the USB interface below it -- so such
# a rule is unsatisfiable and silently never fires. 60-persistent-hidraw.rules
# runs earlier and imports the usb_id builtin, so match its properties instead.
SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", KERNEL=="hidraw*", \
  ENV{ID_USB_VENDOR_ID}=="0d62", ENV{ID_USB_MODEL_ID}=="54bf", \
  ENV{ID_USB_INTERFACE_NUM}=="04", \
  GROUP="input", MODE="0660"

# The keyboard-backlight LED. Normally nothing writes this file directly --
# PowerDevil or UPower do, as root, and going through them is what keeps the
# desktop's brightness slider in step. The rule is for the case where neither
# is running (a bare compositor, a TTY), so omen-fx-brightness has a last
# resort that does not need root. Only the brightness attribute is opened up.
SUBSYSTEM=="leds", KERNEL=="omen::kbd_backlight", \
  RUN+="/bin/sh -c 'chgrp input /sys/class/leds/%k/brightness && chmod 0664 /sys/class/leds/%k/brightness'"
